mindmap
  root((Gerunds))
    The -ing form of a verb
    Gerund as Subject 
      Example: Reading improves vocabulary.
      Example: Traveling is exciting.
    Gerund as Object
      After certain verbs
        Example: I enjoy swimming.
        Example: She avoids eating junk food.
        Common Verbs
          enjoy
          avoid
          consider
          suggest
          finish
          keep
    Gerund after Prepositions
      Example: He is interested in learning English.
      Example: She apologized for being late.
      Common Prepositions
        in
        on
        about
        for
        after
    Gerund vs Infinitive
      Change in Meaning
        Example: I stopped smoking. "quit".
        Example: I stopped to smoke, meaning. "paused to do it".
      Memory Difference
        Example: She remembered sending the email. "recall memory".
        Example: She remembered to send the email. "did not forget".
    Fixed Expressions
      Example: It's no use complaining.
      Example: I can't help laughing.
      Example: There's no point in waiting.
